  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q6_PatchPanel
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: Why does the punch-down job work position 1 through 8 in order rather
    than in whatever order is convenient?
  choices:
  - The tool only fits the block in that direction
  - The panel records the order electronically
  - The colour sequence is what the standard defines, and the link fails if it is
    not followed
  - It uses less cable
  correctChoiceIndex: 2
  points: 10
  explanation: "Position on the block is position on the pin. Two conductors swapped
    there are a split pair or a reversed pair on the finished link \u2014 faults
    a basic continuity check can miss, but that a certifier and a real network will
    not."
